      "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n## Overview\n\nCorrect WNA16 block-count adjustment before increasing BLOCK_SIZE_K. Related to #52590; awaiting consolidation with the directly overlapping #52634.\n\n## Claims\n\n- The existing patch fixes the no-op division and includes a block-configuration regression.\n- No new code commit was made in the 2026-10-15 audit because #52634 implements the same arithmetic correction.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Re-read #52590, compared the existing patch with #52634, and inspected current main `c5f8adc0`, where the assignment still precedes the division.\n- No fresh test, model evaluation, main-sync commit or push is claimed for this unchanged PR head.\n\n## Details\n\nBoth PRs fix the same issue by moving the division before `block_size_k = 256`; #52634 also has regression coverage. Per AGENTS.md's duplicate-work rule, further competing implementation work is deferred pending maintainer guidance. Open since 2026-08-18; the request is to choose/consolidate an implementation so the shared fix can advance.\n\nAI assistance was used for this audit and the original contribution. Human review and any required GPU validation remain necessary.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [ ] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n**BEFORE SUBMITTING, PLEASE READ <https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/contributing>**\n",
